==Changelog March 27th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Easter 2024'''

* Easter has arrived with a good old-fashioned mystery to unscramble. Catch up with the Easter Bunny outside the Grand Exchange to start the egg hunt.
* Added new Easter rewards, including fetching FashionScape and a new Book…

'''Varlamore: Part One Feedback Changes'''

* Tweaked the look of the World Map around the moonlight antelopes.
* Corrected the blocking of one tile on Ralos' Rise.
* The Hunter Skill Cape and Max Cape menus now refer to their teleport options as ‘Hunter Areas’ rather than ‘Chinchompa Teleports’.
* Rebalanced the bosses from Perilous Moons:
** The Eclipse Moon boss now has slightly higher Defence.
** The Blue Moon boss builds Cold twice as fast.
** The Blue Moon boss heals more consistently during the Tornado phase.
** The Blood Moon boss’ healing from its third attack has been reduced.
** The Blood Moon boss’ healing from the Jaguar attacks has increased slightly.
* Removed a bush from the Sunlight Antelope area that prevented them from following players.
* The Fishing activity in the Perilous Moons dungeon now interrupts repeatable actions like Fletching.
* Corrected the description for Doom to state that it applies on ''any'' damage taken, rather than any damage taken 'off-Prayer'.
* Players can now toggle receiving duplicate Hunter Rumours. This toggle is ‘ON’ by default but can be changed using the ‘Rumour-Settings’ option on Verity.
* The naming of Rumours, Loot Sacks and Skill Guide references are now consistent and should reference Basic, Adept, Expert and Master tiers.
* Rotated the north and east traps to face the Pyre Foxes and increased the number of Pyre Foxes in the area.
* Improved the appearance of all Pitfall Trap creatures.
* Hunting for Red Chinchompas now correctly tells you to retrieve Fur.
* Razor-Backed Kebbit meat can now be stored in Meat Pouches.
* Obtaining Sunfire Splinters from Sunlight Antelopes will now correctly add them to the Collection Log.
* Reduced the respawn timer for Sunlight and Moonlight Antelopes.
* Players world hopping while Thieving in the Bazaar will now be able to do so faster.
* Fixed an issue where a Medium Anagram Clue behaved like a Challenge Scroll instead of a Clue Scroll.
* Made more trees across the Avium Savannah choppable.
* Fixed an issue where players couldn’t permanently disable the warnings inside Perilous Moons.
* Increased the buy limit of Atlatl Darts at the Grand Exchange.
* The Eclipse Atlatl’s requirements are now 50 Attack and Strength.
* The Master Clue that required the Fortis Salute now requires a normal Salute instead.
* One fish is now guaranteed when Fishing in Perilous Moons, although two fish can be obtained with a skill check.

<u>'''Previous Hotfixes'''</u>

* Extended the range of Sol Heredit's Spear Strike and Shield Slam attacks.
* Restored Yew Trees to their usual spots.
* Players can no longer walk inside the walls of the Varlamore Crypt.
* The skeleton north of the Colosseum now gives the correct note.
* Players are now able to craft the Hunter Sunlight Crossbow when boosting to level 74 Fletching.
* Removed the interaction message when trying to combine Spear Tips and Headless Arrows.
* Players can once again teleport to Al Kharid via the Jewellery Box, and right-click options should work again.
* Hunter creatures now drop Rumour items as intended.
* Improved the drop rates for some Hunter Rumour items.
* Removed Herblore XP for creating Moonlight Potions inside Perilous Moons.
* Fixed a S.T.A.S.H. Unit in Fortis.
* Increased the maximum permitted player count inside the boss rooms for each of the Moons of Peril.
* Reduced the healing offered by Snowy Knight Mixes.
* Fixed a bug where the new Quetzal pet could not be reclaimed from Probita.
* Apatura will now correctly offer to unlock the teleport to the Hunter Guild.
* The bosses from Perilous Moons will now render on top of anything else in their rooms.
* Fixed an interaction where Dizana's Quiver and Toxic Blowpipe weren’t respecting the bonuses offered by the Blowpipe's ammunition.
* The reduction for Colosseum Death Costs will now apply up to 100 completed waves.
* Echo Boots no longer lose charges in PvP – considering they don’t work there, we feel this makes sense.
* Players will now receive a message about the Quetzal Whistle and where to claim it when they complete 10 Rumours.
* Reduced the XP given for creating Sunfire Runes, which now correctly give XP per Essence used.
* Prevented Random Events from spawning in the houses associated with the Thieving activity.
* You will no longer receive duplicate Huntsman's Kits from Hunter Loot Sacks.
* Moonlight Moths, Sunlight Moths and Snowy Knight Jars now have the same delay as other potions.

'''Other Changes'''

* Improved the accuracy of spells cast by Kolodion and the other arena mages, after a previous error made them less accurate than they should have been. Protect from Magic still provides protection from their spells.
* The Account Guide on Tutorial Island no longer advises Jagex Account users to link emails to their accounts, as they no longer need to do that.
* If you have not unlocked the Bones to Peaches spell, it can now be hidden by the Spellbook filter that hides spells you lack the requirements to cast.
* Players doing the Lassar section of Desert Treasure II can now recover lost quest items from Ketla.
* Changed the sound effect on the mage Vardorvis head attack to something shorter. Thanks to Aatykon and his Twitch chat for the help picking it out.
* Crossbow Bolts will now activate at the correct rate of 10%.

'''PvP Rota'''

The PvP rota has moved to '''Period B''':

* 560 - (UK) - PvP World
* 319 - (US) - Bounty Hunter World
* 579 - (US) - High-Risk PvP World
* 561 - (UK) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 580 - (US) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Zerker</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.
