==Easter 2024 ==
[[File:Easter & Varlamore Updates (1).png|600px|center]]

The Easter Bunny has arrived in Gielinor once more, but his baskets are looking a little bare...

Oh dear. It seems chocolate eggs are in short supply this Easter, and the people of Varrock are ''not'' happy bunnies about it. This warrants an invest-egg-ation!

A rather scrambled Easter Bunny has set up shop just outside of the Grand Exchange in Varrock, so head on over to help him crack the case of the missing choccies.

As always you’ll be rewarded for your efforts with a selection of seasonal goodies, including some rather smashing FashionScape and, of course, some Easter Eggs!

We hope you’re as egg-cited for this event as we are…

==Varlamore: Part One Feedback Changes==
We’ve had a relatively smooth landing in the Shining Kingdom of Varlamore! It’s been great to watch you all explore this beautiful new land and uncover all that Part One has to offer. Here’s an updated breakdown of some of the stats from launch week:

[[File:Easter & Varlamore Updates (2).png|600px|center]]

As with any major update, we had a few post-launch changes and fixes to make. You can find last week’s hotfixes in the Changelog up top, so we’ll move swiftly on to this week’s changes.

===Fortis Colosseum===
Just a small fix to the description of Doom, which now correctly states that the effect applies on ''any ''damage taken, not just damage taken ‘off-Prayer’.

Stay tuned for more Colosseum changes soon!

===Hunter Guild===
Excellent news for confused hunters this week! We’ve tweaked the names of Loot Sacks to indicate which tier of Hunter’s Rumours they came from.

For those of you who prefer a little variety, we’ve added a toggle which prevents you receiving the same Hunter’s Rumour back-to-back. It’s toggled ‘ON’ by default, but you can change it using the new ‘Rumour-Settings’ option on Guild Scribe Verity.

The Hunter Skill Cape and Max Cape menus now correctly refer to their teleport options as ‘Hunter Areas’, rather than ‘Chinchompa Teleports’.

Outside the Guild, Sunlight and Moonlight Antelopes will now respawn much faster, and we’ve switched up the scenery to stop them getting stuck on bushes and the like. Additionally, your Collection Log will now update correctly when receiving Sunfire Splinters from these springy creatures. Finally, the World Map should look a bit more aesthetically pleasing in the area around the Moonlight Antelopes.

Pyre Foxes have had a look over too and we've shifted the Traps in the North and East of the area to face where the Foxes like to hang out. Not only that, but we've also seen more Pyre Foxes within that region!

We’ve also made a small fix to the Red Chinchompa Rumour, which now correctly tells you to bring back Red Chinchompa Fur.

Finally, we’ve improved the overall look of various Pitfall creatures so that you’ll have a better time removing them from the area.

===Perilous Moons===
Top of the list, some balancing tweaks for the bosses:

* The Eclipse Moon boss now has slightly higher Defence.
* The Blue Moon boss builds Cold twice as fast.
* The Blue Moon boss heals more consistently during the Tornado phase.
* The Blood Moon boss’ healing from its third attack has been reduced.
* The Blood Moon boss’ healing from the Jaguar attacks has increased slightly.

Next up, the Fishing activity now interrupts repeatable actions like Fletching so you can remain focused on the task at hand. Speaking of which, we’ve made it clearer that Fishing guarantees one fish, although you can obtain two fish with a successful skill check.

We’ve seen PvPers making use of the Eclipse Atlatl with great results! To make things a bit fairer (and prevent lower brackets being dominated by the Obsidian Maul), we’ve rebalanced the required stats to 50 Attack and Strength.

Last but not least, we’ve fixed a bug where players were being persistently warned of the dangers of the Perilous Moons dungeon even after deciding to ignore them. Don’t worry, you weren’t forgetting to check the box – we were just looking out for you a bit aggressively.

===Miscellaneous===
* Corrected the blocking of one tile on Ralos' Rise.
* Players world hopping while Thieving in the Bazaar will now be able to do so faster.
* Fixed an issue where a Medium Anagram Clue behaved like a Challenge Scroll instead of a Clue Scroll.
* More trees across the Avium Savannah should now be choppable!
* Increased the buy limit of Atlatl Darts at the Grand Exchange.
* The Master Clue that requires players to perform the Fortis Salute with the Blue Moon Set equipped now requires a regular Salute instead.

==Other Changes==
* Improved the accuracy of spells cast by Kolodion and the other arena mages, after a previous error made them less accurate than they should have been. Protect from Magic still provides protection from their spells.
* The Account Guide on Tutorial Island no longer advises Jagex Account users to link emails to their accounts, as they no longer need to do that.
* If you have not unlocked the Bones to Peaches spell, it can now be hidden by the Spellbook filter that hides spells you lack the requirements to cast.
* Players doing the Lassar section of Desert Treasure II can now recover lost quest items from Ketla.
* Changed the sound effect on the mage Vardorvis head attack to something shorter. Thanks to Aatykon and his Twitch chat for the help picking it out.
* Crossbow Bolts will now activate at the correct rate of 10%.

